Refresh tokens

Current: login issues only an access token (`signAccessToken` / `JWT_SECRET` /
`JWT_EXPIRES_IN`). `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET` and `JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES_IN` are already
in env but unused. When the access token expires the user must log in again.

Changes
- Issue a refresh token at login (separate secret and longer TTL).
- Add `POST /auth/refresh` to mint a new access token from a valid refresh token.
- Store refresh tokens (or their hashes) so they can be revoked on logout and
  when a user is disabled.
- Rotate refresh tokens on use; reuse of an old token should revoke the family.
- Do not put refresh tokens in localStorage if the client can use httpOnly
  cookies; do not log tokens.
- Keep access tokens short-lived; `requireAuth` continues to verify only the
  access token.

